# Data Dictionary – `bank_transaction.csv`

## Overview
`bank_transaction.csv` contains sample bank transaction data for multiple users.  
Each row represents a single transaction associated with a specific bank account.

## File Description
- **File name:** `bank_transaction.csv`
- **Data type:** Transaction-level financial records
- **Use cases:**  
  - Transaction analysis  
  - User spending behavior  
  - Financial categorization and aggregation  

## Column Definitions

| Column Name  | Description                                  |
|-------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `client_id` | Unique identifier for the user               |
| `bank_id`   | Unique identifier for the bank               |
| `account_id`| Unique identifier for the bank account       |
| `txn_id`    | Unique identifier for the transaction        |
| `txn_date`  | Date the transaction was posted              |
| `description` | Text description of the transaction        |
| `amount`    | Monetary value of the transaction            |
| `category`  | Example category assigned to the transaction |

## Notes
- All identifiers are assumed to be unique within their respective domains.
- Transaction amounts may be positive or negative depending on transaction type.
- Categories are illustrative and may not represent standardized taxonomies.
